### 1. Login first (sets {{jwt}} for all requests below)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

> {%
   client.global.set("jwt", response.body.token);
 %}

### 2. Create a plant WITH tags
POST http://localhost:8080/api/owned
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}

{
  "nickname": "Tag Test Plant",
  "description": "Testing tags",
  "lastWatered": "2026-03-01T00:00:00Z",
  "waterFrequency": 7,
  "trefleId": 1,
  "tagNames": ["cactus", "kitchen"]
}

> {%
   client.global.set("plantId", response.body.id);
 %}

### 3. Get all tags for the current user
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tags
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}

### 4. Get the plant — verify tags appear in the response
GET http://localhost:8080/api/owned/{{plantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}

### 5. Patch the plant — replace tags (adds "living-room", removes "kitchen")
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/owned/{{plantId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}

{
  "tagNames": ["cactus", "living-room"]
}

### 6. Patch the plant — clear all tags (send empty list)
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/owned/{{plantId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}

{
  "tagNames": []
}

### 7. Patch the plant — omit tagNames entirely (tags should stay unchanged)
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/owned/{{plantId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}

{
  "nickname": "Tag Test Plant Renamed"
}

### 8. Create a second plant with a shared tag to test filtering
POST http://localhost:8080/api/owned
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}

{
  "nickname": "Another Cactus",
  "description": "Also has the cactus tag",
  "lastWatered": "2026-03-01T00:00:00Z",
  "waterFrequency": 14,
  "trefleId": 1,
  "tagNames": ["cactus"]
}

### 9. Get all owned plants — both plants' tags should appear in the response
GET http://localhost:8080/api/owned?page=0
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}
